{"name":"String Cheese","hex":"#fbf1dd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"string cheese","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various cheeses that can be peeled in strings or strips."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/string_cheese"}],"entries":[{"title":"String cheese","blocks":[{"text":"String cheese is any of several different types of cheese where the manufacturing process aligns the proteins in the cheese, making it stringy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/%C3%9Aden%C3%BD_korb%C3%A1%C4%8Dik_%28Slovakia%29.jpg/330px-%C3%9Aden%C3%BD_korb%C3%A1%C4%8Dik_%28Slovakia%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/String_cheese","wikidata":"Q5761746"},{"title":"String","blocks":[{"text":"String is a long flexible tool made from fibers twisted together into a single strand, or from multiple such strands which are in turn twisted together. String is used to tie, bind, or hang other objects. It is also used as a material to make things, such as textiles, and in arts and crafts. String is a simple tool, and its use by humans is known to have been developed tens of thousands of years ago. String may also be a component in other tools, and in devices as diverse as weapons, musical instruments, and toys. The ubiquity of string as a tool has led to conceptual and scientific uses of the term, including strings in computer science, cosmic strings, and string theory."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Length_of_string.jpg/330px-Length_of_string.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/String","wikidata":"Q11064354"},{"title":"Cheese","blocks":[{"text":"Cheese is a type of dairy product produced in a range of flavors, textures, and forms by curdling of milk, usually from cows, goats or sheep, and sometimes of water buffalo. During production, milk is usually acidified and either the enzymes of rennet or bacterial enzymes with similar activity are added to cause the protein casein to coagulate. The solid curds, consisting of proteins and milkfat, are then separated from the liquid whey and pressed into finished cheese. Some cheeses have aromatic molds on the outer layer or rind, while others have them throughout."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Cheese_platter.jpg/330px-Cheese_platter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheese","wikidata":"Q10943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/%D4%B9%D5%A5%D5%AC_%D5%BA%D5%A1%D5%B6%D5%AB%D6%80_2.jpg/500px-%D4%B9%D5%A5%D5%AC_%D5%BA%D5%A1%D5%B6%D5%AB%D6%80_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/%D4%B9%D5%A5%D5%AC_%D5%BA%D5%A1%D5%B6%D5%AB%D6%80_2.jpg/1280px-%D4%B9%D5%A5%D5%AC_%D5%BA%D5%A1%D5%B6%D5%AB%D6%80_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/%D4%B9%D5%A5%D5%AC_%D5%BA%D5%A1%D5%B6%D5%AB%D6%80_2.jpg/500px-%D4%B9%D5%A5%D5%AC_%D5%BA%D5%A1%D5%B6%D5%AB%D6%80_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Armenian traditional tel panir","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%D4%B9%D5%A5%D5%AC_%D5%BA%D5%A1%D5%B6%D5%AB%D6%80_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/String_Cheese_%287973943306%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-String_Cheese_%287973943306%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/String_Cheese_%287973943306%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-String_Cheese_%287973943306%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_